# Trivy exceptions for the messaging-api image.
#
# CVE-2025-47273 (setuptools, HIGH): FALSE POSITIVE — verified 2026-11-03.
# Evidence:
#   1. A root-filesystem search of the built image for *.dist-info, *.whl,
#      *.egg-info AND *70.3.0* / *0.45.1* / *5.3.0* finds NO setuptools
#      (see the workflow's "Locate stale dist-infos" diagnostic output).
#   2. Trivy's own scanned Python target list contains no setuptools
#      dist-info or egg-info.
#   3. The phantom setuptools@70.3.0 appears identically on both
#      python:3.11.18-slim and python:3.12.16-slim-bookworm bases, while
#      neither image contains the package — it is not in the image's files.
# The package does not exist in the image, so the vulnerability cannot be
# exploited. Re-evaluate this exception if the base image changes or if a
# future Trivy DB corrects the detection.
CVE-2025-47273
